        "embedding_dimension": 1024,
        "full_text": "1.1 Introduction\nThe design and implementation of relational databases forms the core of modern software\narchitecture.\nOur database system utilizes a structured relational database architecture where data is organized into\ntables or relations.\n1.2 System Architecture\nThe system consists of a query parser, relational algebra optimizer, storage engine, and a concurrency\ncontroller.\nThis architecture guarantees that the database engine can manage tables, indexes, and tuples\nefficiently.\nWe represent schema definitions and database architecture elements cleanly to provide transactional\nintegrity."
      }
