        "embedding_dimension": 1024,
        "full_text": "2.1 Formal Definition of Operators\nRelational Algebra Selection and Projection Operators are the principal operators utilized to prune and\nretrieve data.\nThe selection operator filters rows based on a given predicate, whereas the projection operator filters\ncolumns.\nBy executing projection, we construct a new relation containing only the requested attributes.\nBy combining selection and projection operators, queries can be optimized before execution.\n2.2 Algebraic Optimization\nQuery optimization involves rewriting relational algebra expressions into equivalent and more efficient\nforms.\nThis compiler translates SQL Select Queries into relational algebra expression trees for direct\noptimization."
      }
    },
