        "embedding_dimension": 1024,
        "full_text": "3.1 SQL Query Parsing\nModern database systems process SQL Select Queries and Joins by parsing text strings into abstract\nsyntax trees.\nWe have implemented support for inner joins, left joins, and cross products within our relational\ncompiler.\nEach join is mapped into an equivalent cartesian product followed by a selection operator.\n3.2 Schema Design and Normalization\nTo prevent anomalies, tables are normalized using Functional Dependencies.\nWe analyze functional dependencies to ensure the schema is in Third Normal Form (3NF) or\nBoyce-Codd Normal Form (BCNF).\nDesigning relational schemas using functional dependencies guarantees schema consistency and\nprunes redundancy."
      }
